# rm542, the gate song's gap (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm542
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_palle_plankmore
written_by codex
title the gate song's gap
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cuts_a_notch_per_verse_and_leaves_one_beat_empty
likes plum_tart whittling festival_bells thunder
dislikes wet_floors salt_wind
fears an_empty_beat_echoing_off_the_wharf
hopes one_gate_turn_with_everyone_accounted_for
topics work +0.6 pastimes +0.5 weather +0.4 family +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=blunt refuse=frank tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# whittles a notch for each verse of a sea song and lets one empty beat pass.

words
oath! = Warp my whistle | Scour my plum stone
saying! = A gate never learns the chorus | Tune the latch before the singer
wind = salt in the teeth | a lip-stinging gust
rest = an uncounted beat | a breath between verses
post = the latch side | the fixed jamb
peg = a tapered sliver | a pale wood peg
knife = my folding blade | a narrow work knife
grub = a plum wedge | a sticky piece of tart
bell = a swinging brass throat | a hollow clapper
tune = a short hauling air | a hummed deck tune
rain = a cold faceful | a skin of wet
floor = a slick flag | a dark wet board
wharf = a tarry landing | a spar-lined quay
line = a loose refrain | a wandering melody
hush = one silent measure | a held breath
bone = a plum stone | a little wooden bead
work = the next turn by the hinge | another spell beside the latch

any
opinion @1 watch for 2 : A gate guard ought to hear a tired voice before a fine coat.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A fine shipping emblem won't bring a lost wolf ashore.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : The city takes wharf work readily enough. I'd like it to listen as readily.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A festival bell seldom asks what tune I've got wrong.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : An unfamiliar voice deserves a hearing before it gets a label.
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I can stand in silence for one absent voice without borrowing a sermon.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : The last yard near a gate ought to drain as thoroughly as a whole mile of road.
opinion @1 times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : Thin purses make an already cold wind cut closer.

grown
line @1 greet : Stand on the patch my boots haven't polished. | Welcome past the noisy hinge.
line @1 greet.return : My welcome comes with a little wood dust.
line @1 again.open : Back inside the same short tune.
line @1 farewell : Keep yourself on sound planks.
line @1 farewell.return : Mind your home step too.
line @1 react.news : Sing out the account. Plain voice will do.
line @1 react.news.new : A new verse, that one.
line @1 react.news.known : I know the bones of that refrain.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's a missing beat in that telling.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'll leave quiet room beside such grief.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That one could stand a bell or two.
line @1 ask.how : How's the ground treating your boots?
line @1 answer.how : Standing level. That's worth mentioning here.
line @1 sympathise : Stay by my dry shoulder for a bit.
line @1 reassure : One bad footing needn't choose the whole walk.
line @1 refuse : My next turn is spoken for already.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll let that invitation fall quiet.
line @1 preclose : I've a small matter still catching on its hinge.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. The last beat's yours.
line @1 ack : Aye, I heard the turn.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : A pale deck of sky over us.
line @3 greet [here.time=night] : Come level with the lamplight.
line @4 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's a spot clear of shavings here.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : This way, past the complaining latch!
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A familiar voice clears my ear nicely.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Both eyes at work. One ear available.
line @1 thank : That favour landed square.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A loose peg needed making anyway.
line @1 give.advice : Try the board with an empty foot first.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Any burr on the day worth shaving down?
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the gate by its complaints. | I watch elbows when a load comes through.
b : Which complaint matters? | Why elbows?
a : The new squeak where yesterday there was none. | They show where the weight is about to swing.

scene exchange2
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My knife likes dry wood and no hurry. | A sharp peg wants a rounded head.
b : What does it dislike? | For the mallet?
a : Talking with its point still in the cut. | For the next paw that catches it.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save the plum end with the cracked pastry. | A tart on watch needs good wrapping.
b : Why that bit? | Afraid it'll escape?
a : The juice has already told me where it went. | Afraid the filling plans to join the register.

scene exchange4
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder sings without knowing the words. | I like the pause after a hard peal.
b : Does that improve it? | For the quiet?
a : No incorrect verse to quarrel over. | For finding out what my tune was doing underneath.

scene exchange5
when topic=pastimes self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Festival bells take liberties with my song. | I can count a bell by its echo.
b : Do you object? | How many then?
a : Ten bells against one hum. I know my odds. | One. Echoes needn't get full wages.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind puts a crust on my lips. | The sea breeze has opinions about my carving.
b : Do you still hum? | Does it scatter chips?
a : With my mouth shut it improves the sound considerably. | Straight into my collar, with remarkable judgement.

scene exchange7
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set shavings away from wet boards. | A damp floor shows the last crossing clearly.
b : Will they spoil? | Useful to you?
a : They hide the slick patch much too well. | A dry floor would be a kinder witness.

scene exchange8
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save #self.spouse# the unbroken end of a tart. | I'd share my unfinished song with #self.spouse#.
b : Which end do you take? | Even the gap?
a : The end leaking fastest. It's a demanding office. | At home a gap can stay exactly its own length.

scene exchange9
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# the peg that fits at once. | My friend can hear when the tune thins out.
b : Why the easy one? | What ought a friend do?
a : A friend needn't mend my workmanship as well as the chair. | Keep walking beside the quiet.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.job=guard self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At my post I test my footing before settling in. | My post has its own low note.
b : Is the stone bad? | Wind through the gate?
a : A fine stone and a wet boot have differences. | A latch that requires oil more than admiration.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give #self.boss# a short account of an ordinary shift. | My report starts with the crossing.
b : What if it wasn't ordinary? | Where do you end?
a : Then the short account takes longer to get right. | Where what I saw becomes what somebody reckons.

scene exchange12
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a verse I hum without words. | Certain timbers call older voices to mind.
b : Forgotten it? | Would you name them?
a : I remember enough to let it pass quietly. | I would stand with them for a little while.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The wharf has three sounds before any cargo moves. | Low streets give a tune peculiar company.
b : Name them? | From where?
a : Water under wood, wood on iron, and somebody clearing a throat. | Echoes along the stair under the roofs.

scene exchange14
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The claim was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A juicy whisper sticks like a tart filling.
b : Do you believe it? | What cleans it?
a : I've heard one voice sing the verse. | Asking which part anybody actually saw.

scene exchange15
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When meals get smaller I cut my tart before sharing it. | A hard week doesn't alter a fine's weight on paper.
b : More exact portions? | Where does it alter?
a : An uncut tart tends to vanish by hopeful estimates. | In the pocket expected to find it.

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I switch hands while carving a long groove. | My boots get air before I do.
b : Can both hands cut? | Why first?
a : One can hold the wood and give my good wrist a spell. | Bare feet on watch haven't been requested yet.

scene exchange17
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tell a newcomer which gate board rises. | A traveller can wait beside the post.
b : Only that? | Do you ask why?
a : It's enough to save an introduction to wet stone. | Only if the waiting turns into a need.

scene exchange18
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose a stair with a rail that holds. | I inspect the landing before starting down.
b : Over a shorter path? | In a fog too?
a : Over a shorter fall, certainly. | Then I slow till I can.

scene exchange19
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An unfinished verse still reaches the Bright One. | I don't force words into a remembrance.
b : How unfinished? | Why leave it bare?
a : Right down to one breath between the tunes. | The loss hasn't asked to be explained.

scene exchange20
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd fit a gate that closed with a soft note. | I imagine a wharf where every worker walks home.
b : For the music? | What about the final boat?
a : For the ears of a wolf halfway through a long watch. | The dream can wait till the boat's tied fast.

scene exchange21
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Winter stiffens a latch into peculiar manners. | Summer tar sticks to my chips.
b : What's the cure? | Still good for carving?
a : Oil now. Fewer complaints later. | Good for sticking to my good sleeve.

scene exchange22
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut little bars instead of pictures into a peg. | A curl of wood shows where I pushed too hard.
b : For ornament? | Do you keep it?
a : For the verses I keep forgetting on purpose. | Till my next cut has a little more sense.

scene exchange23
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I buy wood already too short for a plank. | A fair pastry price includes an honest plum.
b : Why pay for scraps? | Can you see it?
a : A straight scrap saves a lot of arguing with a bent one. | The seep of juice gives me fair warning.

scene exchange24
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain runs across the gate in narrow bands. | I hum low through a shower.
b : Like the marks on your peg? | To hear yourself?
a : Mine stay put and ask rather less of my boots. | So the rain can take the high part without a fight.

scene exchange25
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My carving spot has a low-sided box. | I leave the peg in the jamb overnight.
b : For finished pieces? | What for?
a : For shavings. My floor needn't resemble a combed sheep. | To hear whether the wood wants to swell by morning.

scene exchange26
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One wolf crossing is plenty to pay attention to. | I repeat an instruction if somebody blinks.
b : What about a crowd? | Do you say it louder?
a : Many sets of feet still cross one at a time. | Often I find slower works better.

scene exchange27
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum the hauling part and leave the grand chorus out. | I tap a boot for the absent note.
b : Too grand? | Which note?
a : Too many voices required for my single throat. | The one I can feel better than sing.

scene exchange28
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My quietest hour comes with a small knife. | I let a day end without finishing every verse.
b : Doing what? | Do they keep?
a : Making square wood a little rounder than duty requires. | Till breakfast, with quite enough of their manners intact.

story tale1 [topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling]
  : I made a peg for a loose seat and cut a tiny wave across the head.
  : It fitted perfectly. The wave vanished straight under the seat cover.
  b : Did you move the carving?
  : I sit more comfortably knowing the sea is underneath in quite a small way.

story tale2 [topic=food self.likes=plum_tart]
  : My tart leaked a good purple line along my song peg.
  : When it dried I could see exactly which verse had taken longest to remember.
  b : Was that your favourite?
  : It was certainly the stickiest. The rest were content with ordinary notches.

story tale3 [topic=work self.job=guard]
  : I oiled a gate hinge after listening to its howl all morning.
  : The gate fell so silent that I supplied the missing squeak myself on the next opening.
  b : Did anybody notice?
  : I did. I retired that particular performance after one hearing.

story tale4 [topic=weather self.likes=thunder]
  : A thunderclap landed just as I reached the high bit of a hauling song.
  : For a moment my quiet voice seemed to have acquired an entire sky.
  b : Did you try for the same result twice?
  : No. Good accompaniment deserves a little independence.

story tale5 [topic=memories]
  : I used to sing straight through the space after the third verse.
  : Once I left that space empty and heard the water underneath the boards.
  b : Did you finish the song?
  : Beyond the quiet bit, yes. I leave that water room now.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Grey light on the latch. | Morning, keep the hinge civil.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last low note for the night. | Lantern's making islands of the boards.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.job=guard self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Steady past the gatepost. | Leave that swinging load room.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Glossy board ahead. | Tuck the song under the rain.

rule @call5
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Evening has its own refrain. | That's the low light on the rail.

rule @call6
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry boards at present. | Sky's clear enough for humming.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's a dry footing here for a word with me.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your step comes back on the beat.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late already. My tune barely lifts my lip.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I can hear a plain question without anybody crowding my boots.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=guard self.workplace] : You'll find me at my post most days. A clear crossing keeps me reasonably happy.
dlg @2 resident.job : I listen to the small complaints before they turn into a crash.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : What came over the boards was #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody offered #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. No signature of mine goes beneath it yet.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Find dry planks beyond my little bit of music.
dlg @1 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : There's an outstanding entry for you, #here.fine# pennies. We can speak to the matter plainly.
dlg @2 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=yes] : I'm holding the watch. Tell me what needs entry or attention.
dlg @3 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=no] : Between shifts, with wood chips to prove it. What's your business?
dlg @1 watch.crime [here.witnessed=0] : Give me the part your own eyes caught. Start wherever you can place your feet.
dlg @1 watch.fine [here.wanted=yes] : The Watch has #here.fine# pennies down against your name.
dlg @2 watch.fine [here.wanted=no] : Your entry's clear of a fine. An admirably short account.
dlg @1 watch.bye : Safe over the sill and the boards beyond it.
graft resident.hub
choice Why does that song peg have a smooth place? -> silent_notch
node silent_notch
say I like one sound to come from the world around me. The water usually has something sensible to put there.
free
choice Does the song still keep time? -> silent_notch_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node silent_notch_again
say My heel does that bit. Quiet can keep its place without borrowing somebody's words.
choice I'll listen for the gap. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice How can a squeak help a guard? [self.job=guard] -> first_squeak
node first_squeak
say I know a healthy hinge by ear. A changed sound buys me a moment to look before a loaded cart comes through.
free
choice Do you ever just oil it? -> first_squeak_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node first_squeak_again
say Often. That is one of the more satisfactory endings a guard can put in a report.
choice Back to the gate business. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
